<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>9.10.2: Expanding from Factored Form to Standard Form</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02499</md:content-id>
    <md:title>9.10.2: Expanding from Factored Form to Standard Form</md:title>
    <md:uuid>e613e98c-3c47-4de8-8d8b-231d057b2969</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Recall learning how to identify and factor perfect square trinomials in Unit 6. Here are some perfect squares in factored and standard forms, and an expression showing how the two forms are related.</para>
<para>Study the first few examples in rows 1 and 2. Create a similar table to the one modeled below. Copy the table (or use a copy provided by your teacher) and then complete the missing numbers in rows 3 – 6 in the rest of the table.</para>
<table class="os-raise-wideadjustedtable">
  <tgroup cols="4"><tbody><row>
      <entry><emphasis>Row</emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>Factored Form</emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis> </emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>Standard Form</emphasis></entry></row>
  <row>
      <entry>
        <para>1</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <para>\((x+4)^2\)</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <para>\((1x)^2+2(1x)(4)+4^2\)</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <para>\(x^2+8x+16\)</para>
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        <para>2</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <para>\((2x+5)^2\)</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <para>\((2x)^2+2(2x)(5)+5^2\)</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <para>\(4x^2+20x+25\)</para>
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        <para>3</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <para>\((3x-4)^2\)</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <para>\((3x)^2+2(\_\_\_\;x)(\_\_\_)+(\_\_\_)^2\)</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <para>\(9x^2−24x+16\)</para>
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        <para>4</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <para>\((5x + \_\_\_)^2\)</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <para>\((\_\_\_\;x)^2+2(\_\_\_\;x)(\_\_\_)+(\_\_\_)^2\)</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <para>\(25x^2+30x + \_\_\_\)</para>
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        <para>5</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <para>\((kx+m)^2\)</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <para>\((\_\_\_\;x)^2+2(\_\_\_\;x)(\_\_\_)+(\_\_\_)^2\)</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <para>\((\_\_\_)^2x^2+ \_\_\_\;x+ (\_\_\_)^2\)</para>
      </entry>
    </row>
  </tbody></tgroup></table>

<list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated">
  <item>Enter the missing values from row 3.</item>
</list>
<table class="os-raise-wideadjustedtable">
  <tgroup cols="4"><tbody><row>
      <entry><emphasis>Row</emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>Factored Form</emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis> </emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>Standard Form</emphasis></entry></row>
  <row>
      <entry>
        <para>3</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <para>\((3x-4)^2\)</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <para>\((3x)^2+2(\_\_\_\;x)(\_\_\_)+(\_\_\_)^2\)
          \((3x)^2+2(\;\underline{\;\mathbf a\boldsymbol.\;}\;x)(\underline{\;\mathbf b\boldsymbol.\;})+(\underline{\;\mathbf c\boldsymbol.\;})^2\)</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <para>\(9x^2−24x+16\)</para>
      </entry>
    </row>
  </tbody></tgroup></table>

<section class="check-understanding"><title>Warm Up Activity</title><exercise id="dad71f78-dfbe-4ce8-84f6-174d080677d9" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter the missing value of a.</para><para>What is the missing value of a?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! 3</para><para>The correct answer is 3.</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="f8bd948f-e55c-410a-a56c-08a864670510" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter the missing value of b.</para><para>What is the missing value of b?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! -4</para><para>The correct answer is -4.</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_448b88de-78d0-428d-8320-b5d463cd72fe" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter the missing value of c.</para><para>What is the missing value of c?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! -4</para><para>The correct answer is -4.</para></solution></exercise></section>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated">
  <item>Enter the missing values from row 4.</item>
</list>
<table class="os-raise-wideadjustedtable">
  <tgroup cols="4"><tbody><row>
      <entry><emphasis>Row</emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>Factored Form</emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis> </emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>Standard Form</emphasis></entry></row>
  <row>
      <entry>
        <para>4</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <para>\((5x + \_\_\_)^2\) 
          \((5x + \underline{\;\mathbf a\boldsymbol.\;})^2\)</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <para>\((\_\_\_\;x)^2+2(\_\_\_\;x)(\_\_\_)+(\_\_\_)^2\)
          \((\underline{\;\mathbf b\boldsymbol.\;}\;x)^2+2(\underline{\;\mathbf c\boldsymbol.\;}\;x)(\underline{\;\mathbf d\boldsymbol.\;})+(\underline{\;\mathbf e\boldsymbol.\;})^2\)</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <para>\(25x^2+30x + \_\_\_ \)
          \(25x^2+30x + \underline{\;\mathbf f\boldsymbol.\;}\)</para>
      </entry>
    </row>
  </tbody></tgroup></table>

<section class="check-understanding"><exercise id="a6b625d4-10aa-4150-ae58-791cf77361d7" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter the missing value of a.</para><para>What is the missing value of a?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! 3</para><para>The correct answer is 3.</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="d92d34c8-3b69-4bb0-b4de-ef514d6ed71b" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter the missing value of b.</para><para>What is the missing value of b?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! 5</para><para>The correct answer is 5.</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="eaa30f11-95c5-4267-a258-982376579f21" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter the missing value of c.</para><para>What is the missing value of c?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! 5</para><para>The correct answer is 5.</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_3b4c63db-6340-4d1c-86e9-ade95ce69455" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter the missing value of d.</para><para>What is the missing value of d?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! 3</para><para>The correct answer is 3.</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_1572d1cf-b757-4b6f-a8a0-e625692b3f7a" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter the missing value of e.</para><para>What is the missing value of e?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! 3</para><para>The correct answer is 3.</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_8a1ec2b2-3c19-48e7-9802-3a07306b4efd" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter the missing value of f.</para><para>What is the missing value of f?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! 9</para><para>The correct answer is 9.</para></solution></exercise></section>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated">
  <item>Enter the missing values from row 5.</item>
</list>
<table class="os-raise-wideadjustedtable">
  <tgroup cols="4"><tbody><row>
      <entry><emphasis>Row</emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>Factored Form</emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis> </emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis>Standard Form</emphasis></entry></row>
  <row>
      <entry>
        <para>5</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <para>\((kx+m)^2\)</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <para>\((\_\_\_\;x)^2+2(\_\_\_\;x)(\_\_\_)+(\_\_\_)^2\)
          \((\underline{\;\mathbf a\boldsymbol.\;}\;x)^2+2(\underline{\;\mathbf b\boldsymbol.\;}\;x)(\underline{\;\mathbf c\boldsymbol.\;})+(\underline{\;\mathbf d\boldsymbol.\;})^2\)</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <para>\((\_\_\_)^2x^2 + \_\_\_\;x + (\_\_\_)^2\)
          \((\underline{\;\mathbf e\boldsymbol.\;})^2x^2 + \underline{\;\mathbf f\boldsymbol.\;} x + (\underline{\;\mathbf g\boldsymbol.\;} )^2\)</para>
      </entry>
    </row>
  </tbody></tgroup></table>

<section class="check-understanding"><exercise id="_4605d8cb-adc0-47e9-9ddc-e7b5f0e8a1db" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter the missing value of a.</para><para>What is the missing value of a?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(k\)</para><para>The correct answer is \(k\).</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="d0547d87-7153-4f40-9a1b-06ba89b584bf" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter the missing value of b.</para><para>What is the missing value of b?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(k\)</para><para>The correct answer is \(k\).</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="e65eb74e-65af-419b-8402-a7feb616f885" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter the missing value of c.</para><para>What is the missing value of c?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(m\)</para><para>The correct answer is \(m\).</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_37175167-199e-4386-a447-8ea590d9bf66" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter the missing value of d.</para><para>What is the missing value of d?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(m\)</para><para>The correct answer is \(m\).</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_165fc1b2-9a9c-4672-be9f-506c9a8e9c4c" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter the missing value of e.</para><para>What is the missing value of e?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(k\)</para><para>The correct answer is \(k\).</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_7f40aa1b-830a-44d8-9b8b-72ec21ac5abc" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter the missing value of f.</para><para>What is the missing value of f?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(2km\)</para><para>The correct answer is \(2km\).</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_3b96c095-cbc3-4a4c-8611-b264e978aefa" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter the missing value of g.</para><para>What is the missing value of g?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(m\)</para><para>The correct answer is \(m\).</para></solution></exercise></section>
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>Look at the expression in the last row of the table. If \(ax^2+bx+c\) is equivalent to \((kx+m)^2\), how are \(a\), \(b\), and \(c\) related to \(k\) and \(m\)?</para>
    <para>Write down your answer, then select the<emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  
  <para>\(a=k^2\), \(b=2km\), and \(c=m^2\)</para>

</solution></exercise>
</example></section>
</content>
